WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.567
-Welcome back!

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:02.501
-Come on!
-You're here.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.601
You're in New York City!

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:05.434
This is where
it all started for you.

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:07.767
-Oh my gosh, come on,
New York is my baby!

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:09.334
[ Cheering and applause ]
-How does it feel? Come on.

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:10.801
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:14.467
-I wanted to show a photo
that I found of you.

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:16.501
This is your home studio

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:19.067
when you first started out.
Is that possible?

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.701
-Yep.
-Yeah. Look at that.

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:23.400
-That's me.
-And look at the studio.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.000
-That's about 16 years old.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.801
My bedroom was the studio,

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:29.167
so there was
like a bed right here

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:30.834
and then all the gear
and the piano

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:32.133
and that was where I sat.

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:33.200
-So you could touch the piano
-And this is the closet.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.934
-from your bed?
-Yes, from the bed.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.701
Because it was tiny.
This is the closet

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:38.467
and I thought that, in order
to make a vocal booth,

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:41.234
I had to hang blankets,
so this was the blanket.

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:42.567
[ Laughter ]
-That's right.

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:43.767
I love that you did that.

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:46.100
I also have another photo
of the actual studio.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.100
-Yes!
This is major!

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.133
-Do you have any songs
or any samples on here,

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:51.734
on these machines,
that you're like,

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:54.534
"Oh, no. If I ever play that,
it'll be so embarrassing"?

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:56.300
-There's definitely songs
I feel that,

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.300
if I play,
would be embarrassing.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.434
I actually heard one today,
randomly.

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:03.901
My first song was on the
"Dr. Dolittle" soundtrack.

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:04.634
[ Laughter ]
-Really?!

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:05.968
-And it was called

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:07.467
"Rear View Mirror."

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:10.200
And, you know,
it was my first real attempt

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.234
at an official release.

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:14.534
And, when I listen to it now,
I kind of -- I could just --

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:17.601
I can hear all the insecurities
and all the things.

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:19.868
But it's beautiful, right,
insecurities?

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:22.667
-Yeah, you're starting out,
but also, that's a big break.

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:24.334
-It's a big deal.
It's an Eddie Murphy movie.

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:25.934
Let's do it.
-Let's go!

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:27.834
-Let's do it, right?
But now, you are one

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:29.434
of the best-selling artists
in the world

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:30.968
-Thank you.
-and, officially,

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:33.100
you were certified --
I want to say this --

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:36.901
the Most Certified
Female R&amp;B Artist -- ready? --

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:38.567
of the Millennium.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:40.300
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.367
Of the millennium!

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:45.300
-I have to be honest.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.067
I had to look up
the word millennium.

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:48.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.868
You're like, "How many years
is a millennium?"

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:54.701
-"Let me be clear
about what millennium means."

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:56.801
This is major. Millennium is --
-Congratulations.

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:58.634
-I was feeling
really proud of that.

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:00.701
My husband actually
surprised me with it.

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:02.367
Somehow, he got the news first

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:04.200
and I was washing dishes
in the kitchen

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.367
and he comes up over to me
with the camera

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:08.133
and he's always on his phone,

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:09.567
trying to get some type
of video.

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:11.100
You know, those husbands?

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.901
[ Laughter ]
And so I'm washing the dishes
and he comes over

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:14.801
and he has the camera
all in my face.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.200
"So, how do you feel?"

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.767
And I'm like, "Huh?

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:19.167
[ Laughter ]
I'm washing the dishes."

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:21.234
And he's like, "No, really, what
do you feel like right now?"

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:23.601
I was like, "I don't --
I don't -- I'm just --

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:24.767
I'm soapy?
I don't know."

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:26.434
[ Laughter ]
-"I'm soapy.

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:27.934
"What are you up to?"
-And so he finally

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:29.534
broke the news to me
and I was like

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:32.501
so proud, but shy,
but like excited

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:34.434
and I worked
all my life for this.
-Look at this.

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:36.934
Yeah, exactly, right?
-Since that right there!

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.434
[ Cheering and applause ]
-That's where it started.
-Yes!

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:40.801
-That's awesome!
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:42.801
-And you're going on tour
this summer.

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:44.033
-Yes.
-It's a big deal.

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:46.667
-No, it's amazing.
I'm going on tour first time in,

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:49.534
I guess, two years,
since all of the,

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:50.868
you know, I mean, maybe more.

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:53.400
At this point, how long has
the pandemic been like?

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.501
[ Laughter ]
-We all stopped counting.

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:56.868
But, please. We're happy
that you're on tour, though.

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:59.400
-Okay, I'mma be on tour
and, since that,

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.934
it was originally
the Alicia Tour

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:02.534
because that was the album
I put out.

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:05.601
And, since then,
I put out my album called Keys,

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:08.901
so now it's going to be
the Alicia Keys Tour.

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:10.167
-That's what I'm talking
about, yeah.

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:11.267
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:13.133
Yeah, you got to add Keys
in there.

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:16.000
You did it one night
at the Apollo.
-Mm!

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.100
-Did you rub the stump?
Did you do the whole thing?

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.801
-I definitely --
You have to rub the stump.

00:03:19.801 --> 00:03:21.567
If you don't rub the stump...
-Then you're a fool.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.767
-Nah, it's not going to be
a good night.

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.033
-You have to get good luck.
-Yes!

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:26.901
-I mean, how was that?
I know you

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:29.501
had Egypt record something.
What was it?

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.634
-It was
"Somewhere Over the Rainbow."

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:36.000
-No, yeah, that was.
-So, Egypt is my 11-year-old.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.501
-He's 11 already?

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:38.634
That wild, right?
-Crazy.

00:03:38.634 --> 00:03:42.300
-And so he's playing piano
and he's singing

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.901
and he's writing songs
and the whole thing.

00:03:43.901 --> 00:03:46.434
So this was his first song
that he recorded

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:49.167
in the studio with me,
like, you know, singing.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:50.267
-"Somewhere Over the Rainbow."

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:51.767
I mean, it had me
just tearing up

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:53.300
and it's not even my kid.
-Nah.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.267
[ Laughing ] I can imagine.
-I definitely had a moment

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:58.667
where I was like, "Wow!"
Because I realized that

00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:01.634
like his voice is never going
to sound like that again.

00:04:01.634 --> 00:04:03.934
He's never going to have
that place where it's kind of

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:05.234
he hasn't quite hit puberty.

00:04:05.234 --> 00:04:07.534
It's still really sweet.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:11.334
-And I was just witnessing like
a moment in time

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:12.934
that probably
will never come back,

00:04:12.934 --> 00:04:15.167
so, it's really beautiful.

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:16.868
It's so sweet.
You got to hear his voice.

00:04:16.868 --> 00:04:19.901
-And then,
your other baby, Genesis.

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:21.667
-Genesis.

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:23.300
-Does he want to be
in the limelight or he's like,

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.968
"I'm cool"?
-Genesis doesn't like anybody.

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:27.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.767
Okay?
-Doesn't like anybody.

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:31.601
-He's not for the games,
alright?

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:34.934
He's not for any
of the showcasing, no.

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:36.367
Don't take pictures of him.

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:38.934
Don't ask him to like
go be nice to people, no.

00:04:38.934 --> 00:04:40.167
[ Laughter ]
-No, he doesn't do that, no.

00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:42.901
-So he's a little tough guy.
He's a hot pepper.

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:44.400
And so, after the Apollo show --

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.901
It was really
an incredible show.

00:04:45.901 --> 00:04:48.834
It was so electric
and alive and special

00:04:48.834 --> 00:04:50.567
and he was watching
from the side of the stage

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:51.801
because, somehow, the Apollo,

00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:54.334
you have to be over 16
to be in the audience,

00:04:54.334 --> 00:04:56.934
-Is that right?
-which was new --
I didn't realize it.

00:04:56.934 --> 00:04:59.667
So he's at the side
of the stage, you know,

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:02.167
just respectfully
following the rules.

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:04.400
And I come out at the end
of the show and he says,

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.667
"Mommy, why didn't you
bring me out?!"

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:09.667
And I was like, "Who are you?

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:10.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.734 --> 00:05:12.100
What?!
-You go, "You don't do this."

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.734
-You don't even want --" I said,
"Do you want to come out?"

00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:15.167
He's like --
I was like, "Right now?"

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:16.734
He's like --
I said, "Okay.

00:05:16.734 --> 00:05:18.334
I'll do one more song,
so you can come out,"

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:19.667
and he was like, "Okay."

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:22.000
And then, right when I walked,
"But I'm scared now."

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.667
[ Laughter ]
I said, "No, don't be
scared now."

00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:26.334
No, come on, man, let's go."
-"Genesis, you set this up."

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:28.501
We have a little video of you
and Genesis here.

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:30.467
Check this out --
Alicia Keys and Genesis.

00:05:30.467 --> 00:05:34.901
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:36.033
-Hello.

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:38.400
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.334
-I can't -- No.

00:05:39.334 --> 00:05:40.367
[ Cheering and applause ]
-"Hello."

00:05:40.367 --> 00:05:41.734
That's the voice.

00:05:41.734 --> 00:05:44.133
By the way,

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:47.033
I can't believe he was up there
saying hello to anybody.

00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:48.901
-Right?
-Such a shocker.

00:05:48.901 --> 00:05:51.701
So it was sweet to see him
kind of, you know, go for it.

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:53.300
-I love that you brought him.
That's awesome.

